          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em spectral sequence
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algorithm"} algorithm
            or computational tool in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            and more generally in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            which allows to compute
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %em bi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+objects"} graded objects
            from the homology/homotopy of the two graded components.
          %p
            Notably there is a spectral sequence for computing the homology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            from the homology of its row and column complexes separately. This in turn allows to compute
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
            of composite functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\circ F
            from the double complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo •
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo •
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\bullet G (\mathbb{R}^\bullet F(-))
            obtained by non-totally deriving the two functors separately (called the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GrothendieckSpectralSequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            here this gives rise to various important classes of examples of spectral sequences, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SpecialGrothendieckSpectralSequence"} below
          %p
            More concretely, a homology spectral sequence is a sequence of graded chain complexes that provides the higher order corrections to the
            %em naïve
            idea of computing the homology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tot
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tot(V)_\bullet
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\bullet, \bullet}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tot
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tot(V)_\bullet
          %p Being, therefore, an iterative perturbative approximation scheme of bigraded differential objects, fully-fledged spectral sequences can look a bit intricate. However, a standard experience in mathematical practice is that for most problems of practical interest the relevant spectral sequence “perturbation series” yields the exact result already at the second stage. This reduces the computational complexity immensely and makes spectral sequences a wide-spread useful computational tool.
          %p
            Despite their name, there seemed to be nothing specifically “spectral” about spectral sequences, for any of the technical meanings of the word
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+-+disambiguation"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Leray"} Jean Leray
            and has long become standard, but was never really motivated (see p. 5 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Chow"} Chow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            theory/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            that spectral sequences frequently arise by considering the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+diagram"} sequences
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+stable+homotopy+type"} spectral sequence of a filtered stable homotopy type
          %p
            While therefore spectral sequences are a notion considered in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            and more generally in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            variant of the notion in plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+spectral+sequence"} homotopy spectral sequence
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We give the general definition of a (co)homology spectral sequence. For motivation see the example
            %em
              %a{:href => "#SpectralSequenceOfFilteredComplex"} Spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            below.
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %h3#spectral_sequence Spectral sequence
          #CohomologySpectralSequence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong cohomology spectral sequence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a family
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^{p,q}_r)
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q,r
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\geq 1
                %p
                  (for a fixed
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  these are said to form the
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                    \-th page
                  of the spectral sequence)
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q,r
                  as above a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  (called the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %strong differential
                #eq:FormOfDifferentialInCohomologySpectralSequence.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo −
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d^{p,q}_r
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E^{p,q}_r
                        \\longrightarrow
                        E^{p+r,q-r+1}_r
                %p
                  satisfying
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_r^2 = 0
                  (more precisely,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi d
                            %mi r
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mi r
                              %mo ,
                              %mi q
                              %mo −
                              %mi r
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ∘
                          %msubsup
                            %mi d
                            %mi r
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo ,
                              %mi q
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_r^{p+r,q-r+1}\circ d_r^{p,q} = 0
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi α
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_r^{p,q}: H^{p,q}(E_r)\to E^{p,q}_{r+1}
                  where
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+cohomology"} chain cohomology
                  is given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ker
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} im
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi r
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H^{p,q}(E_r) = \mathrm{ker} d^{p,q}_r/ \mathrm{im} d^{p-r,q+r-1}_r
                        \\,.
          %p
            Analogously, a
            %strong homology spectral sequence
            is collection of objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_{p,q}^r)
            with the differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_r
            of degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-r,r-1)
          %h3#ConvergenceOfSpectralSequences Convergence
          #LimitTerm.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^r_{p,q}\}_{r,p,q}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              such that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q
              there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(p,q)
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \geq r(p,q)
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^{r \geq r(p,q)}_{p,q} \simeq E^{r(p,q)}_{p,q}
                    \\,.
            %p Then one says equivalently that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigraded+object"} bigraded object
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                          %mn ∞
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                          %mrow
                            %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E^\infty
                        \\coloneqq
                        \\{E^\infty_{p,q}\}_{p,q} \coloneqq \{ E^{r(p,q)}_{p,q} \}_{p,q}
                %p
                  is the
                  %strong limit term
                  of the spectral sequence;
              %li
                %p
                  the spectral sequence
                  %strong abuts
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi E
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\infty
          #Degeneration.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If for a spectral sequence there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s
              such that all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
              on pages after
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s
              vanish,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo ≥
                          %msub
                            %mi r
                            %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^{r \geq r_s} = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^{r_s}\}_{p,q}
              is a limit term for the spectral sequence. One says in this cases that the spectral sequence
              %strong degenerates
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p By the defining relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mi r
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mi r
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi pq
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^{r+1}_{p,q} \simeq ker(\partial^r_{p-r,q+r-1})/im(\partial^r_{p,q}) = E^r_{pq}
            %p
              the spectral sequence becomes constant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s
              on if all the differentials vanish, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\partial^r_{p,q}) = E^r_{p,q}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q
          #Collaps.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              If for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^r_{p,q}\}_{r,p,q}
              there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi s
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s \geq 2
              such that the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_s
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Degeneration"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitTerm"}
              %strong collapses
              on this page.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \geq 2
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
              of the spectral sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mi r
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mi r
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial^r \colon E^r_{p,q} \to E^r_{p-r, q+r-1}
            %p
              have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              necessarily in different rows an columns (while for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1
              both are in the same row and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 0
              both coincide). Therefore if all but one row or column vanish, then all these differentials vanish.
          #Convergence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^r_{p,q}\}_{r,p,q}
              %strong converges weakly
              to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exhaustive+filtering"} exhaustive filtering
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet H_\bullet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^r_{p,q} \Rightarrow H_\bullet
                    \\,,
            %p
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded"} associated graded
              complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{G_p H_{p+q}\}_{p,q} \coloneqq \{F_p H_{p+q} / F_{p-1} H_{p+q}\}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is the limit term of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitTerm"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\infty_{p,q} \simeq G_p H_{p+q} \;\;\;\;\;\;\; \forall_{p,q}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Furthermore one says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %strong converges
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet
                  is also a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+filtration"} Hausdorff filtration
              %li
                %p
                  %strong converges strongly
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet
                  is also a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Hausdorff+filtration"} complete Hausdorff filtration
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Boardman99"}> Boardman 99, def. 2.5
            ) See also
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+convergence+of+spectral+sequences"} conditional convergence of spectral sequences
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p In practice, spectral sequences are often referred to via their first interesting page, usually the first or the second. Then one often uses notation such as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^1_{p,q} \;\Rightarrow\; H_\bullet
            %p or
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^2_{p,q} \;\Rightarrow\; H_\bullet
            %p to be read as “There is a spectral sequence whose first/second page is as shown on the left and which converges (weakly, strongly, or conditionally) to a filtered object as shown on the right.”
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The nature of the convergence condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
              is well illuminated for instance by the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+skeleton"} skeleta
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mi p
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi im
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^p E^{\bullet}(X) im(  E^\bullet(X,X_{p-1}) \to E^\bullet(X))
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in the
              = succeed "-ground" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^p(X,E^q(\ast)) \Rightarrow E^{p+q}(X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the elements on the left in bidegree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
              are manifestly given by cocycles that trivialize on the
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p-1)
              = succeed "-cocycles)," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mi p
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi im
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^p E^{p+q}(X) = im(E^{p+q}(X,X_{p-1}) \to E^{p+q}(X))
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              In applications one is interested in computing the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n
              and uses spectral sequences converging to this as tools for approximating
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n
              in terms of the given filtration.
            %p
              Therefore usually spectral sequences are required to converge in each degree, or even that for each pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
              there exists an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0
              such that for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\geq r_0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi d
                        %mi r
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mi r
                          %mo ,
                          %mi q
                          %mo +
                          %mi r
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_r^{p-r,q+r-1} = 0
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^r)
              collapses at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n
              being the unique entry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{p,q}^r
              on the non-vanishing row/column with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+q = n
          %h3#Boundedness Boundedness
          #BoundedSpectralSequence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^r_{p,q}\}
              is called a
              %strong bounded spectral sequence
              if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,r \in \mathbb{Z}
              the number of non-vanishing terms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{k,n-k}
              is finite.
          #QuadrantSpectralSequence.num_defn
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E^r_{p,q}\}
              is called
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong first quadrant spectral sequence
                  if all terms except possibly for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q \geq 0
                  vanish;
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong third quadrant spectral sequence
                  if all terms except possibly for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q \leq 0
                  vanish.
            %p
              Such spectral sequences are bounded, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BoundedSpectralSequence"}
          #BoundedSpectralSequenceHasLimitTerm.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A bounded spectral sequence, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BoundedSpectralSequence"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitTerm"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              First notice that if a spectral sequence has at most
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              non-vanishing terms of total degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              on page
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %p
              Therefore for a bounded spectral sequence for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(n) \in \mathbb{Z}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi p
                      %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{p,n-p} = 0
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \leq L(n)
              and all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(n) \in \mathbb{Z}
              such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi q
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{n-q,q} = 0
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \leq T(n)
              and all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %p
              We claim then that the limit term of the bounded spectral sequence is in position
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
              given by the value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{p,q}
              for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo −
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mi q
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mi q
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    r \gt max(  p-L(p+q-1), q + 1 - T(p+q+1) )
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is because for such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              we have
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi r
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mi r
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{p-r, q+r-1} = 0
                  because
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mi r
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p-r \lt L(p+q-1)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ker
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi r
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\partial^r_{p-r,q+r-1}) = 0
                  vanishes;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                            %mo −
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mi r
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{p+r, q-r+1} = 0
                  because
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi q
                          %mo −
                          %mi r
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mi q
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q-r + 1 \lt T(p+q+1)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi im
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo ,
                            %mi q
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(\partial^r_{p,q}) = 0
                  vanishes.
            %p Therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo ,
                                %mi q
                              %mrow
                                %mi r
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo −
                                %mi r
                                %mo ,
                                %mi q
                                %mo +
                                %mi r
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                              %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo ,
                                %mi q
                              %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msubsup
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo ,
                                %mi q
                              %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msubsup
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo ,
                                %mi q
                              %mi r
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    E^{r+1}_{p,q}
                    \&amp;=
                    ker(\partial^r_{p-r,q+r-1})/im(\partial^r_{p,q})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq E^r_{p,q}/0
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq E^r_{p,q}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h3#ExtensionProblem Extension problem
          %p
            Given a spectral sequence, then even if it converges strongly (def.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded"} associated graded
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtered object
            that it converges to, not the filtered object itself. The latter is in each filter stage an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
            of the previous stage by the corresponding stage of the infinity-page, but there are in general several possible extensions (the trivial extension or some twisted extensions). The problem of determining these extensions and hence the problem of actually determining the filtered object from a spectral sequence converging to it is often referred to as the
            = succeed "." do
              %em extension problem
          %p
            More in detail, consider, for definiteness, a cohomology spectral sequence (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohomologySpectralSequence"}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtered
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\bullet H^\bullet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^{p,q} \;\Rightarrow\; H^\bullet
                  \\,.
          %p Then by definition of convergence there are isomorphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_\infty^{p,\bullet} \simeq F^p H^{p + \bullet} / F^{p+1} H^{p + \bullet}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Equivalently this means that there are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequences"} short exact sequences
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to F^{p+1}H^{p +\bullet} \hookrightarrow F^p H^{p +\bullet} \longrightarrow E_\infty^{p,\bullet} \to 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^p H^\bullet
            from knowledge of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{p+1}H^\bullet
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{p,\bullet}
          %p
            In good cases these short exact sequences happen to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequences"} split exact sequences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mo •
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F^p H^{p+\bullet} \simeq F^{p+1} H^{p+\bullet} \oplus E_\infty^{p,\bullet}
                  \\,.
          %p But in general this need not be the case.
          %p
            One sufficient condition that these exact sequences split is that they consist of homomorphisms of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{p,\bullet}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
            (for instance
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-group" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ext"} Ext
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ext
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext^1_R(E_\infty^{p,\bullet},-)
            vanishes, and hence all extensions are trivial, hence split.
          %p
            So for instance for every spectral sequence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            the extension problem is trivial (since every vector space is a free module).
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p The basic class of examples are
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#SpectralSequenceOfFilteredComplex"} Spectral sequences of filtered complexes
          %p
            which compute the cohomology of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtered complex
            from the cohomologies of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded+objects"} associated graded objects
          %p From this one obtains as a special case the class of
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#SpectralSequenceOfADoubleComplex"} Spectral sequences of double complexes
          %p
            which compute the cohomology of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            using the two canonical filtrations of this by row- and by column-degree.
          %p From this in turn one obtains as a special case the class of
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GrothendieckSpectralSequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequences
          %p
            which compute the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\bullet(G \circ F (-))
            of the composite of two functors from the spectral sequence of the double complex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\bullet (F (\mathbb{R}^\bullet G (-)))
          %p
            Many special cases of this for various choices of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            go by special names, this we tabulate at
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#ListOfExamples"} List of examples
              \.
          %h3#SpectralSequenceOfFilteredComplex Spectral sequence of a filtered complex
          %p
            The fundamental example of a spectral sequence, from which essentially all the other examples arise as special cases, is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+stable+homotopy+type"} spectral sequence of a filtered stable homotopy type
          %p
            If a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet
            is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtration
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\bullet C^\bullet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\bullet H(C)
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
          %p
            A filtration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            also gives rise to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded+object"} associated graded object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr(F)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"} cokernels
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Gr(F^\bullet H^\bullet(C)) \neq H^\bullet (Gr(F^\bullet) C)
                  \\,.
          %p
            But the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence associated to a filtered complex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\bullet C^\bullet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⋆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet (Gr(F^\star) C)
            in the page
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{(1)}
            and in good cases converges to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr(F^* H^\bullet(C))
          %h3#SpectralSequenceOfADoubleComplex Spectral sequence of a double complex
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            is naturally filtered in two ways: by columns and by rows. By the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            this gives two different spectral sequences associated computing the cohomology of a double complex from the cohomologies of its rows and columns. Many other classes of spectral sequences are special cases of this cases, notably the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+spectral+sequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
            and
            %em its
            special cases.
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+double+complex"} spectral sequence of a double complex
          %h3#HyperDerivedFunctors Spectral sequences for hyper-derived functors
          %p
            From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+double+complex"} spectral sequence of a double complex
            one obtains as a special case a spectral sequence that computes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-derived+functors"} hyper-derived functors
          %p (…)
          %h3#GrothendieckSpectralSequence Grothendieck spectral sequence
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+spectral+sequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
            computes the composite of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
            from the two derived functors separately.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} \stackrel{F}{\to} \mathcal{B} \stackrel{G}{\to} \mathcal{C}
            be two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functors"} left exact functors
            between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi p
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^p F : \mathcal{D} \to Ab
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            etc. .
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              sends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              to
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+objects"} acyclic objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
              then for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{A}
              there is a
              %a{:href => "#FirstQuadrant"} first quadrant
              cohomology spectral sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_r^{p,q} := (R^p G \circ R^q F)(A)
            %p
              that converges to the right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              of the composite functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_r^{p,q} \Rightarrow R^{p+q} (G \circ F)(A).
            %p Moreover
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge+maps"} edge maps
                  in this spectral sequence are the canonical morphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi p
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        R^p G (F A) \to R^p (G \circ F)(A)
                %p
                  induced from applying
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  to an injective resolution
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to \hat A
                  and the morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi q
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        R^q (G \circ F)(A) \to G(R^q F (A))
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
                  of low degree terms is
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        0 \to (R^1 G)(F(A)) \to R^1(G \circ F)(A)
                        \\to G(R^1(F(A)))
                        \\to (R^2 G)(F(A))
                        \\to R^2(G \circ F)(A)
          %p
            This is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+spectral+sequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Since for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to \hat A
              an injective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\hat A)
              is a chain complex not concentrated in a single degree, we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^p (G \circ F)(A)
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-derived+functor"} hyper-derived functor
              evaluation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^p(G) (F(A))
            %p
              Therefore the second spectral sequence discussed at
              %a{:href => "#HyperDerivedFunctors"} hyper-derived functor spectral sequences
              converges as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (R^p G)H^q(F(\hat A)) \Rightarrow R^p (G \circ F)(A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now since by construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^q(F(\hat A)) = R^q F(A)
              this is a spectral sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (R^p G)(R^q F) A) \Rightarrow R^p (G \circ F)(A)
                    \\,.
            %p This is the Grothendieck spectral sequence.
          %h3#SpecialGrothendieckSpectralSequence Special Grothendieck spectral sequences
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#LeraySpectralSequence"} Leray spectral sequence
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#HochschildSerreSpectralSequence"} Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#BaseChangeSpectralSequence"} Base-change spectral sequence
          %h4#LeraySpectralSequence Leray spectral sequence
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray+spectral+sequence"} Leray spectral sequence
            is the special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+spectral+sequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
            for the case where the two functors being composed are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} push-forward
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            along a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            followed by the push-forward
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to *
            to the point. This yields a spectral sequence that computes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in terms of the abelian sheaf cohomology on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
              be suitable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              be a morphism of sites. () Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = Ch_\bullet(Sh(X,Ab))
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D} = Ch_\bullet(Sh(Y,Ab))
              be the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model categories of complexes of sheaves of abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_Y
              compose to
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_X : \mathcal{C} \stackrel{f_*}{\to} \mathcal{D} \stackrel{\Gamma_Y}{\to} Ch_\bullet(Ab)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh(X,Ab)
              a sheaf of abelian groups on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there is a cohomology spectral sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_r^{p,q} := H^p(Y, R^q f_* A)
            %p that converges as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_r^{p,q} \Rightarrow H^{p+q}(X, A)
            %p
              and hence computes the cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in terms of the cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              with coefficients in the push-forward of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h4#BaseChangeSpectralSequence
            Base change spectral sequence for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tor
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tor
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            for its category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : R_1 \to R_2
            and an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            there are composites of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mi Mod
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 2
                  %mi Mod
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mn 2
                      %mi N
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R_1 Mod \stackrel{\otimes_{R_1} R_2}{\to} R_2 Mod \stackrel{\otimes_{R_2} N}{\to} Ab
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %mi Mod
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mn 1
                          %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 2
                  %mi Mod
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Ab
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R_1 Mod \stackrel{Hom_{R_1 Mod}(-,R_2)}{\to}
                  R_2 Mod
                  \\stackrel{Hom_{R_2}(-,N)}{\to}
                  Ab
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{R_2}(-,N)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 2
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{R_2} N
            are the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ext"} Ext
            = succeed "-functors," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tor"} Tor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+spectral+sequence"} Grothendieck spectral sequence
            applied to these composites yields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change+spectral+sequence"} base change spectral sequence
            for these.
          %h4#HochschildSerreSpectralSequence Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild-Serre+spectral+sequence"} Hochschild-Serre spectral sequence
          %h3#exact_couples Exact couples
          %p
            The above examples are all built on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SpectralSequenceOfFilteredComplex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
            = succeed "." do
              %em exact couples
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couple"} exact couple
            is an exact sequence of three arrows among two objects
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi φ
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{j}{\to} D \overset{\varphi}{\to} D \overset{k}{\to} E \overset{j}{\to}.
          %p These creatures construct spectral sequences by a two-step process:
          %ul
            %li
              first, the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi k
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \coloneqq k j \colon E\to E
              is nilpotent, in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2=0
            %li
              second, the homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,d)
              supports a map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi φ
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j':E'\to \varphi D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                      %mo :
                      %mi φ
                      %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k':\varphi D\to E'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mi φ
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D'=\varphi D
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ′
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi φ
                  %mi D
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ′
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ′
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E' \overset{j'}{\to} D' \overset{\varphi}{\to} D' \overset{k'}{\to} E' \overset{j'}{\to}
                  \\,.
          %p is again an exact couple.
          %p
            The sequence of complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,d),(E',d'),\dots
            is a spectral sequence, by construction. For more see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "exact+couple#SpectralSequencesFromExactCouples"} exact couple – Spectral sequences from exact couples
          %p
            Examples of exact couples can be constructed in a number of ways. Notably there are naturally
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "exact+couple#ExactCoupleOfATowerOfFibrations"} exact couples of towers of (co-)fibrations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequences"} Adams spectral sequences
            are usually produced this way (from towers which are
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+resolutions"} Adams resolutions
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SpectralSequencesInducedFromTowersOfSpectra"} below
          %p
            Importantly, any short exact sequence involving two distinct chain complexes provides an exact couple among their total homology complexes, via the Mayer-Vietoris long exact sequence; in particular, applying this procedure to the relative homology of a filtered complex gives precisely the spectral sequence of the filtered complex described (???) somewhere else on this page. For another example, choosing a chain complex of flat modules
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ˙
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^\dot,d)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}/p^2\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
          %p gives the exact couple
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi β
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(d,\mathbb{Z}/p^2\mathbb{Z})
                  \\overset{[\cdot]}{\to}
                  H^\bullet(d,\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})
                  \\overset{\beta}{\to}
                  H^\bullet(d,\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})
                  \\overset{p}{\to}H^\bullet(d,\mathbb{Z}/p^2\mathbb{Z})\cdots
          %p
            in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is the
            %em
              mod-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              Bockstein
            homomorphism.
          %p
            The exact couple recipe for spectral sequences is notable in that it doesn’t mention any grading on the objects
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D,E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} coker
                    %mi φ
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi ker
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coker \varphi\to E\to \ker\varphi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j,k,\varphi
          %h3#ListOfExamples List of examples
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+diagram"}> tower diagram
                    \/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} filtering
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+stable+homotopy+type"} spectral sequence of a filtered stable homotopy type
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+chain+complex"} filtered chain complex
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+complex"} spectral sequence of a filtered complex
                %tr
